   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's look at what was said.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Люди часто спят.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'People often sleep.' 'People' is an irregular plural. 'They sleep' carries 'yat'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Они не хотят думать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They don't want to think.' 'They want' is irregular, ending in 'yat'. 'To think' is the plain form.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Все любят мечтать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everyone loves to dream.' 'Dream' means to daydream, not to sleep. 'They love' is plural, to go with 'everyone'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Мы видим сны.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We have dreams.' Russians 'see' dreams, where English 'has' them. 'We see' carries 'im'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Такая у нас жизнь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Such is our life.' 'Such at us life' is the word order. There's no 'is'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Никто не видит правду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nobody sees the truth.' 'Nobody' and 'not' appear together. 'Truth' takes a 'u' ending.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Мы сами не видим.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We ourselves don't see.' 'Ourselves' is a short plural word. It comes right after 'we'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Многие закрывают глаза.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Many close their eyes.' 'Eyes' is plural, with a stressed 'a'. 'Many' is plural, too.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Они боятся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They are afraid.' 'Fear' finishes with 'sya', so it's 'they fear themselves'. A short, plain line.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Просто ждут чудо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They just wait for a miracle.' 'Wait for' takes the object form, but 'miracle' is neuter and doesn't change. 'Just' sits at the front.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Никто ничего не знает.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nobody knows anything.' Three negatives: 'nobody', 'nothing' and 'not'. All are required.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "И все молчат.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And everyone keeps quiet.' 'Are silent' carries 'yat'. 'Everyone' is the plain word. Here is the whole conversation again.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
